  ('de28d19d-c2af-5971-a8e6-cd464b277375', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Halima's clove extract shows no effect, she considers dropping data, her mentor explains the value of a clear negative result, and she presents every dish honestly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Halima removes two contaminated dishes, proves cloves preserve bread, and wins the symposium.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"Halima learns that science is boring because most experiments end with no exciting answer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Dr. Morales scrolls through Halima's spreadsheet twice before asking her a question.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Halima's clove extract shows no effect, she considers dropping data, her mentor explains the value of a clear negative result, and she presents every dish honestly.$q$, $q$The correct choice covers the failed result, the temptation, the mentor's guidance, and her honest poster without judging. The passage says the dishes were not contaminated and never mentions winning.$q$, 'draft', '6e07af05-c302-5308-bdee-146ba797d760')
