   $q$How does the second stanza prepare for the poem's theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows the speaker still believes the cranes are abandoning the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains the scientific reasons cranes migrate north in spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"It reveals that the speaker dislikes the river and wants to move north.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It redefines home as a whole route rather than one fixed place, an idea the speaker later applies to leaving.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It redefines home as a whole route rather than one fixed place, an idea the speaker later applies to leaving.$q$, $q$The speaker moves from "they were leaving us" to "Their home is the whole long road between," preparing the realization about the speaker's own departure. "Now I know" shows the old belief has changed.$q$, 'draft', 'b5945d61-2ba0-5c29-8d89-fade7d73d655')
