   $q$After taking out sentence 12, the report has no ending. Which sentence would be the best concluding statement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A burrow is a hole or tunnel that an animal digs in the ground for a home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-one-detail"},{"text":"Some people also like to build snowmen in their yards in the winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Winter is very boring, so I wish it could be summer all year long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-tone-opinion"},{"text":"Whether they fly away, grow warm coats, or sleep for months, animals have smart ways to get through winter.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Whether they fly away, grow warm coats, or sleep for months, animals have smart ways to get through winter.$q$, $q$A concluding statement sums up the main ideas, and this one brings together all three ways from the report: moving away, growing a coat, and sleeping. The burrow sentence only repeats one definition from the last paragraph, so it does not wrap up the report.$q$, 'draft', 'e23bc942-92a8-5bee-bf87-857895f8e7ac')
