        '3-5', $q$From Cotton Plant to T-Shirt$q$, $q$(1) Cotton is soft. (2) Many T-shirts are made from cotton, a plant that grows on farms. (3) A boll is the round pod on a cotton plant that holds the fluffy cotton.

(4) Farmers pick the cotton after the bolls burst open. (5) Next, the cotton must be cleaned. (6) ___ a machine called a cotton gin pulls out the seeds. (7) Then other machines comb the cotton to take out dirt and bits of leaves.

(8) After that, the clean cotton is spun into thread. (9) Spinning means twisting the fibers together to make one long, strong strand. (10) Machines knit or weave the thread into cloth. (11) Workers cut the cloth and sew the pieces into shirts. (12) One big bundle of cotton, called a bale, can make more than a thousand T-shirts. (13) My favorite shirt has a picture of a tiger on it.$q$, 'draft')
