  ('0b78db7a-8908-5232-8c00-e1062c21c19e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g3-opinion-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to join sentences 8 and 9 with a linking word. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bikes are also better for the air than cars because fewer cars on the road would mean less smoke and noise.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Bikes are also better for the air than cars, or fewer cars on the road would mean less smoke and noise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-linking-word"},{"text":"Bikes are also better for the air than cars, but fewer cars on the road would mean less smoke and noise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-word-misused"},{"text":"Bikes are also better for the air than cars until fewer cars on the road would mean less smoke and noise.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-linking-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bikes are also better for the air than cars because fewer cars on the road would mean less smoke and noise.$q$, $q$Sentence 9 explains why bikes are better for the air, so "because" correctly links the reason to its explanation. "But" is wrong because the two ideas agree with each other; they do not contrast.$q$, 'draft', '655162e4-f20c-52cf-af22-3418d5e5221b')
