   $q$The writer wants to add one more reason before sentence 11. Which sentence best supports the opinion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Cars and trucks can travel much faster than bikes do on River Road.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-other-side"},{"text":"A bike path would also give families a free and fun place to spend time together outside.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some people who live in Pine Hollow do not own a bike at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weakens-opinion"},{"text":"Bike helmets come in many sizes, so every rider can find one that fits.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A bike path would also give families a free and fun place to spend time together outside.$q$, $q$Only the sentence about families having a free and fun place to spend time gives a new reason the town should build the path. The sentence about people without bikes is about the topic, but it makes the writer's opinion weaker instead of supporting it.$q$, 'draft', '655162e4-f20c-52cf-af22-3418d5e5221b')
