   $q$The draft has no concluding statement. Which sentence would be the best one to add at the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In conclusion, staying safe in the water is the most important thing for every kid to know.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-too-narrow"},{"text":"That is why every family should go to the beach at least once this summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-opinion"},{"text":"Swimming keeps kids safe, makes them strong and helps them make friends, so every third grader should learn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Swimming is the most fun sport in the whole world, and I could swim all day long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-claim-not-restating"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Swimming keeps kids safe, makes them strong and helps them make friends, so every third grader should learn.$q$, $q$A strong conclusion repeats the opinion and sums up the reasons, and only the sentence naming safety, strength and friends does both. The sentence about staying safe is tempting, but it leaves out two reasons and never restates that third graders should take lessons.$q$, 'draft', 'cd118af1-78db-52c4-968a-cf666c745a60')
